  "explanation": {
    "short": "Albanian has letters of its own. ë is a short, weak \"uh\" (and at the end of a word it is often hardly said). ç is ch as in \"church\". sh is as in \"ship\"; dh is the th of \"this\"; th is the th of \"think\".",
    "more": "sh, dh and th are single letters of the Albanian alphabet, not two letters stuck together: dhe starts with one sound, dh. Albanian is spelled as it sounds, so once you know these letters you can say any word you see."
  },
